OL,3,CHeat health alerts coming into force
OL,4,Cas UK braces for fifth heatwave
OL,6,FThis summer has been one of extreme
OL,7,Fheat and dry conditions, with two
OL,8,Frecord-breaking heatwaves in May and
OL,9,FJune that led to the deaths of more
OL,10,Fthan 2,800 people, followed by further
OL,11,Fheatwaves in July.
OL,13,FThe UK is increasingly struggling with
OL,14,Fthe impact of more extreme weather
OL,15,Fsuch as drought, heatwaves and
OL,16,Fwildfires fuelled by climate change,
OL,17,Fwhich is mostly caused by burning
OL,18,Ffossil fuels in power plants, in
OL,19,Fvehicles, to heat homes and for
OL,20,Findustry.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G7/9
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,306,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30508
SC,0008
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F305A1786434481
OL,3,CHeat health alerts coming into force
OL,4,Cas UK braces for fifth heatwave
OL,6,FSome 45 million people are in drought-
OL,7,Fstricken areas, and 27 million
OL,8,Fcustomers are under hosepipe bans as
OL,9,Frivers and reservoirs run low.
OL,11,FFarmers have warned of a "brutal
OL,12,Fharvest" for crops and a lack of feed
OL,13,Ffor livestock, and there have been
OL,14,Fwarnings of food price inflation
OL,15,Fshocks later in the year as a searing
OL,16,Fsummer across Europe feeds through
OL,17,Ffrom fields to supermarket shelves.
OL,26,@sD@ZOUtD@HO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G8/9
